    {
      "id": "EkKceYFKnfB3--dQprC2u",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -17.79095725999889,
      "y": 5130.51863848452,
      "width": 2129.9306640625,
      "height": 700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3x",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1422013976,
      "version": 1953,
      "versionNonce": 2060345704,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1761488097954,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Low Latency:\n    - upload chunks parallely\n    - CDN ?\n        - might be overkill\n        - since users download their own files mostly, the stored files are not accessed frequently\n            - hence storing them on CDN is costly just when one user is going to access that file.\n    - compress & decompress chunks. Compression algo varies for file type.\n    - Delta sync for content updates download i.e when a small change is done to big file, just identify which chunks got effected \n        and only upload/download them. (Discussing impl of this would be difficult within time, but can just say this line )\n        - supported only for client apps , as web apps are not synced to any folder in filesystem\n        - Delta sync is actually a manual download , but when user clicks download/save for offline , only delta gets downloaded.\n            - Its not talking about metadata sync.\n        - Delta sync vs collaborative editing:\n            - Delta sync to sync local files with cloud & vice-versa\n            - Collaborative editing:\n                - when you click on a txt file in client app or web app, it redirects to docs and starts a collaborative session.\n                - ex: 3 users share a file. 2 are updating the file locally, & as and when they make a change\n                    that will be sent to drive & to all users part of the collaborative session i.e 2 users here. But to the 3rd users\n                    these changes (metadata changes will be synced by periodic poll) & ( content changes will be downloaded manually which applies delta sync).\n    ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. Low Latency:\n    - upload chunks parallely\n    - CDN ?\n        - might be overkill\n        - since users download their own files mostly, the stored files are not accessed frequently\n            - hence storing them on CDN is costly just when one user is going to access that file.\n    - compress & decompress chunks. Compression algo varies for file type.\n    - Delta sync for content updates download i.e when a small change is done to big file, just identify which chunks got effected \n        and only upload/download them. (Discussing impl of this would be difficult within time, but can just say this line )\n        - supported only for client apps , as web apps are not synced to any folder in filesystem\n        - Delta sync is actually a manual download , but when user clicks download/save for offline , only delta gets downloaded.\n            - Its not talking about metadata sync.\n        - Delta sync vs collaborative editing:\n            - Delta sync to sync local files with cloud & vice-versa\n            - Collaborative editing:\n                - when you click on a txt file in client app or web app, it redirects to docs and starts a collaborative session.\n                - ex: 3 users share a file. 2 are updating the file locally, & as and when they make a change\n                    that will be sent to drive & to all users part of the collaborative session i.e 2 users here. But to the 3rd users\n                    these changes (metadata changes will be synced by periodic poll) & ( content changes will be downloaded manually which applies delta sync).\n    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
