    {
      "id": "djZ6lfirHNjq-65wjeVBm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8232.367674242756,
      "y": -180.81671330723407,
      "width": 997.859375,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1504240388,
      "version": 992,
      "versionNonce": 1606879804,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1761893553136,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Indexes:\n    \n    Queries: \n        - ChatMember Table:\n            - getAllUsersForChat : \n                - no secondary index neede. Leftmost rule on primary key enough\n                for efficient retrieval.\n            - getAllChatsForUser:\n                - secondary index on (userId , chatId )\n                    - Note: why not index just on userId ?\n                        - Its slower becoz rows has to be fetched after filtering i.e all \n                            realted pages to be loaded to get the chatids. If we store chartId also \n                            as part of the index, chatId is directly stored on BTree node and no need\n                            for page loading.\n        - For rest all tables, primary index is enough or maybe you can create a hash index if you want \n            even better speed. But secondary indexes are not required. \n            \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Indexes:\n    \n    Queries: \n        - ChatMember Table:\n            - getAllUsersForChat : \n                - no secondary index neede. Leftmost rule on primary key enough\n                for efficient retrieval.\n            - getAllChatsForUser:\n                - secondary index on (userId , chatId )\n                    - Note: why not index just on userId ?\n                        - Its slower becoz rows has to be fetched after filtering i.e all \n                            realted pages to be loaded to get the chatids. If we store chartId also \n                            as part of the index, chatId is directly stored on BTree node and no need\n                            for page loading.\n        - For rest all tables, primary index is enough or maybe you can create a hash index if you want \n            even better speed. But secondary indexes are not required. \n            \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
