    },
    {
      "id": "h7TFm6FqZpHbm4R0hTYsS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -6013.345335751711,
      "y": 2199.8578414696976,
      "width": 809.8552856445312,
      "height": 280,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b74",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1864420204,
      "version": 930,
      "versionNonce": 714700908,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1761977607394,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- = 1B/100k noti per sec = 10k reads/sec to postgres\n- postgres capability = 10k TPS, 100k QPS (simple read)\n    - so primary can handle this, no read-replicas needed\n    - so no sharding also needed, as writes to db are the no. of signups \n        which is very minimal\n- 1 simple read from postgres = 1ms (same as reading 1mb from ssd, here not 1mb but \n                                            Btree traversal or query processing time will nullify it)\n    - can speed it up to 4x using cache (0.25ms reading 1mb from cache)\n- add indexes \n- Notification servers can be scaled how much ever we want \n    to meet the throughput of services.\n-  3rd party services might not able to handle this much throughput & we dont have control over them.\n    - Hence can use message queues to apply backpressure - TODO \n- Read bookv1 - TODO",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- = 1B/100k noti per sec = 10k reads/sec to postgres\n- postgres capability = 10k TPS, 100k QPS (simple read)\n    - so primary can handle this, no read-replicas needed\n    - so no sharding also needed, as writes to db are the no. of signups \n        which is very minimal\n- 1 simple read from postgres = 1ms (same as reading 1mb from ssd, here not 1mb but \n                                            Btree traversal or query processing time will nullify it)\n    - can speed it up to 4x using cache (0.25ms reading 1mb from cache)\n- add indexes \n- Notification servers can be scaled how much ever we want \n    to meet the throughput of services.\n-  3rd party services might not able to handle this much throughput & we dont have control over them.\n    - Hence can use message queues to apply backpressure - TODO \n- Read bookv1 - TODO",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
